ndamentally we know that high  literacy  is the best guarantee of both academic  and eventually professional success not  for everyone but statistically  overwhelmingly and if that's the case  if you are teaching in a school don't  worry  about all these learning styles which  has been debunked by the way it's you  just go google you know learning fads  learning styles is a fad for that matter  critical thinking is a fad you'll find  lots of serious  studies that debunk all of this  and instead the focus should be on  teaching people to read and if you're a  language learner focus on becoming a  good reader in the language that you're  learning now maybe all you need to do is  exchange a few pleasantries or you don't  want to go to the trouble of learning  chinese characters  fine but you're going to miss out  ultimately you won't you'll only be able  to go so far so  that's what i wanted to say today about  about the importance of reading  and because reading is so important and  should be the focus of any teaching  program therefore i think this  getting sidetracked into learning styles  and teaching critical thinking is only a  smokescreen a distraction from the  fundamental  task the teaching of the fundamental  skill  reading  there you have it i just thought i'd get  that off my chest today so bye for now
 

